reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:4:// ValSeqs (Python dict order; keys distinct; re-inserting a key updates its value in place, keeping
reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:5:// the original position). Concrete for krun (the ordered build + `.keys()` are the real ops); a proof
reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:6:// over a SYMBOLIC dict passes `dictV(KS, WS)` with a symbolic key sequence KS and reads
reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:7:// `d.keys() = list(KS)`, then keeps each key opaque problem-locally.
