codex
The reference semantics contains a defined `eval(str)` specifically for this HumanEval task, including Python precedence and right-associative exponentiation. I’ll use the standard one-loop construction: append each operand/operator pair, append the final operand, then call `eval`. The proof domain will be one symbolic recursive input object, which represents every finite valid pair of lists—not bounded lengths.
apply patch
patch: completed
/workspace/solution.py
