codex
The implementation now avoids symbolic slicing/indexing: it pairs every operand with the corresponding operator plus one final empty operator. That keeps the unbounded proof structural. I’m compiling the untouched reference semantics with LLVM and running four precedence-sensitive concrete cases before drafting the symbolic configuration.
