The repaired unbounded loop invariant now closes with `#Top`. Its base case models zip truncation exactly, and its recursive case threads the actual projected integer/string values. I’m moving to the exact module-load/function-call claim now; this is where allocation, binding, return/pop, and the fixed `evalArith` result all have to line up.
